# Build-context excludes for server.Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` before falling back to a
# `.dockerignore` at the context root — which is how this file can live under
# infra/ while the build context is the repository root. Every pattern below is
# therefore relative to the REPO ROOT, not to infra/.
#
# Without this, the whole repo (Gradle caches, node_modules, .git) would be
# uploaded to the daemon on every build.

.git
.gitignore

# Host-built artifacts: the image builds its own.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build

# Nothing in the image comes from these.
android
dashboard/src
dashboard/index.html
dashboard/vite.config.ts
docs
infra

# Secrets must never enter a layer. .env.example is fine, real .env files are not.
**/.env
**/.env.local

*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
